1
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:31,639
To all patrolling air units.
A 208 is in progress...

2
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,472
...in the C-13 district
of Newport City.

3
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:37,109
The airspace over this area
will be closed. Repeat:

4
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,158
To all patrolling air units.
A 208 is in progress...

5
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,191
...in the C-13 district
of Newport City.

6
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:45,352
The airspace over this area
will be closed. Repeat...

7
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,156
There's nothing
to worry about.

8
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:17,158
You can try it again once
you're in our country.

9
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,111
"Try it again?"

10
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,953
Just as there's no such thing
as a bug-free program...

11
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:26,039
...there's no program
that can't be debugged.
Am I wrong?

12
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:28,151
You don't understand.

13
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,879
We still don't know if
it really is a bug.

14
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,389
Project 2501's
original purpose was--

15
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:36,438
Major, Section 6
is ready to move in.

16
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:40,869
- Major!
- I hear you.

17
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:45,072
There's a lot of
static in your brain.

18
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,310
It's that time
of the month.

19
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:58,193
Won't there be trouble
if Section 9 butts in
on Section 6's operation?

20
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:00,316
That diplomat's a pretty
well-known bastard.

21
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:03,955
Even if they catch him there,
all they can do is deport him.

22
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:09,108
We're the only ones
who can get our hands dirty.

23
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,834
They're moving.
Take us over to
the extraction point.

24
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:52,350
What? The police?

25
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,115
Stop it! Who told you to
open fire?! Drop your guns!

26
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:11,717
I have diplomatic immunity!
Let me see who's in charge!

27
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:14,115
Transporting a listed programmer
out of the country...

28
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,196
...violates our
arms export treaty.

29
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:20,108
I could also have you
charged with kidnapping.

30
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,151
Give the man up.

31
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,874
I'm afraid not. He's applied
for political asylum with us...

32
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,793
...and he's already signed
a statement to that effect!

33
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:30,639
- When?!
- I don't have to tell you!

34
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,479
By right of international law,
my country can...

35
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:36,512
...offer him protection
and right of safe passage.

36
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,756
The document is on file
at our embassy.

37
00:03:38,840 --> 00:03:40,990
I'll transfer a copy to you
in a few days.

38
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:43,634
Are you sure about this?
They won't take you back alive.

39
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,870
I must ask that you
watch what you say.

40
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,195
Our country is
a peace-loving democracy.

41
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,271
Is that a fact?

42
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:54,076
Out the window! Shoot!

43
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:05,034
Thermoptic camouflage...

44
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:56,354
This is a rare pleasure,
Mr. Aramaki.

45
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:59,073
What can the Foreign Ministry
do for Section 9?

46
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,156
What are these secret talks
you've scheduled with...

47
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,236
...the Gavel Republic
for tomorrow?

48
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,351
The usual. Foreign aid.

49
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:08,318
The new government
reopened the request
after the revolution.

50
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,954
They claim to be
more democratic...

51
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,833
...but they'll probably be
as bad as the last bunch.

52
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,434
Giving them money
they don't earn
will help nobody.

53
00:09:16,520 --> 00:09:19,114
They consider it reparation
for past exploitation
and won't thank--

54
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:21,435
And what will
the government do?

55
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,159
The problem is that
we have the leader of...

56
00:09:24,280 --> 00:09:26,748
...the old junta here
looking for political asylum.

57
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,711
Col. Maless, right?

58
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:31,872
So, do we throw him out
and grant them the aid?

59
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,231
Or do we publicly
recognize him as a refugee
and cut the aid?

60
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:38,079
Not an easy decision
to make.

61
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:41,272
Personally, if I could find
a politically acceptable
reason...

62
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:44,710
...I'd have the man deported
in a heartbeat.

63
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:57,276
Oh yes, thanks for your help
with that programmer defection.

64
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:00,113
Nakamura over in Section 6
said he was grateful.

65
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:03,158
After all,
we in the diplomatic corps
have to keep our hands clean.

66
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,191
Accessed.

67
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:14,033
We've lost response.
How's her brainwave output look?

68
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:17,596
Normal.
Switching over the virtual
experience mode pattern.

69
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,036
The Foreign Minister's
interpreter.

70
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:25,591
23 minutes ago,
her cyber-brain was hacked
via telephone connection.

71
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:30,113
Just as Foreign Intelligence
division predicted...

72
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:32,156
...the Puppet Master
has begun to break into...

73
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:34,191
...every terminal
on the network.

74
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,709
Pattern analysis shows
a high probability that...

75
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,872
...he's attempting to disrupt
secret talks with Gavel.

76
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,037
We've placed everyone attending
the talks under surveillance.

77
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:45,549
Probably trying
to hack her ghost...

78
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:48,996
...so she'll kill
people at the meeting.

79
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:53,835
How long till he hacks
through her protection
and reaches her ghost?

80
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:58,590
He's using an old-style HA-3.
I'd say about two hours.

81
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,551
After that,
we'll have to cut the line
to eliminate all risk.

82
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:03,956
Batou and Ishikawa
are in a car,
tracing the signal.

83
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,071
Rendezvous with them.

84
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:27,556
The Puppet Master...
That phantom hacker, right?

85
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:29,875
They think
he's an American.

86
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,753
Age, sex, personal history...
Everything about him is unknown.

87
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,872
Since last winter he's been
mainly active in the EC.

88
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,673
Internationally wanted
on dozens of charges of...

89
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:41,479
...stock manipulation,
spying, political engineering...

90
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:45,109
...terrorism, and violation
of cyber-brain privacy.

91
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:48,351
He's ghost-hacked
so many people
to carry out his crimes...

92
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:50,994
...he's earned the code name
"The Puppet Master."

93
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,793
This is the first instance
of him operating
in this country.

94
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:58,158
So, if he's so hot,
why's he using an old HA-3?

95
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:03,798
Well, a newer type
would be less detectable
and be harder to trace.

96
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:09,074
But it could also implicate
the former junta leader,
Col. Maless.

97
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:14,114
So he's using an older type
to keep us from suspecting him.

98
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:18,591
Or somebody else
wants us to think that.

99
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:22,076
Maless may just be another pawn
in this whole thing.

100
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:26,079
Now you're overthinking this.
There's no evidence of that.

101
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,792
Evidence?

102
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:32,598
I just have a whisper...
A whisper from my ghost.

103
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:35,672
By the way, are you
still using that revolver?

104
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:38,678
Afraid both guns
in a two-man team'll jam up?

105
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:40,557
I like the Matever.

106
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:42,711
Since I depend on your backup,
I think stopping power is...

107
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:45,075
...more important than
personal preference.

108
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,156
Especially since it's
my ass on the line.

109
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:49,914
Use the Zastaber instead.

110
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:53,396
Major, I've been
meaning to ask you.

111
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:57,075
Why'd you ask for a guy
like me to be transferred
in from the police?

112
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:58,593
Because you're
a guy like you.

113
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:00,193
Huh?

114
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:05,189
An honest cop with a clean
record. And you've got
a regular family.

115
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:09,472
With the exception of
your cyber-net implants,
your brain's real.

116
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,989
No matter how powerful
we may be fighting-wise...

117
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:14,913
...a system where
all the parts react
the same way...

118
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,197
...is a system
with a fatal flaw.

119
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,793
Like individual,
like organization.

120
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,269
Overspecialization
leads to death.

121
00:13:22,400 --> 00:13:23,435
That's all.

122
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,914
- Come on!
- All right!

123
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:45,229
We're already 40 seconds
behind schedule!

124
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:48,670
- Gimme five more seconds.
- Of all the lousy luck...

125
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,713
Hey, sorry.

126
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:59,792
My last partner,
the one they busted
for working without...

127
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,269
...a permit,
was a better worker than you!

128
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:07,114
You're actually trying
to ghost-hack your own wife...

129
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,231
...just to see
what's on her mind?

130
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:13,831
She doesn't have any time for me
and now she wants a divorce.

131
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:16,957
On top of that, my daughter,
my only child...

132
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:19,310
...thinks I'm cheating
on her mother!

133
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:22,790
So how'd you get your hands
on cracking software?

134
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:27,710
From some programmer.
A really nice guy
I met in a bar.

135
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:30,792
I told him my wife's lawyer
was keeping me
from seeing her...

136
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:32,632
...and he said he'd help.

137
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:35,399
Told me to access
from different places
to keep from getting caught.

138
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,351
Smart guy, huh?

139
00:14:42,360 --> 00:14:44,874
Asshole! Ya tryin' to
get yourself killed?!

140
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:47,679
Looks like we aren't
the only busy people out here.

141
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:53,431
Nobody here.

142
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,835
What's the point?
Even if we trace the calls...

143
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:58,554
...the guy's already gone
by the time we get there.

144
00:14:58,640 --> 00:15:01,393
- Vicious cycle, huh?
- Quit complaining!

145
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,954
Kusanagi and Togusa
are headed for the next
expected hack point.

146
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,190
You two look
for something there.

147
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,719
Look for what?

148
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:09,956
Anything.

149
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,270
Fuckin' old coot.
He tells US to snoop around?!

150
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,436
Wait a sec!

151
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:16,676
Damn, missed him.

152
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,519
Hey, Pops. Did you see
a garbage truck go by here?

153
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:21,596
Who wants to know?

154
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,711
Did you see it or not?

155
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:27,509
Yeah, but they were gone
by the time I got my trash.

156
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:30,194
One was using the phone,
so I thought I had time--

157
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:36,112
Uh, can you take this
to them?

158
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:40,318
A garbage truck? Of course...
They move every seven minutes.

159
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:44,558
Control! Get me
the trash collection
routes for that sector!

160
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:58,514
There are eight garbage trucks
operating in the target area.

161
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:01,194
Target is a type C
collection truck, #79.

162
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:06,555
Let me drive.

163
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,468
Ishikawa, check out
the drivers' homes.

164
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,194
Batou, you get to their
next stop before they do!

165
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:24,478
He may be in contact
with someone else.
Observe, but don't move in!

166
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:26,591
Route data accessed.

167
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:31,111
Hacking points traced
and matched. Target
now stopped at next point.

168
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:35,315
Confirm access via HA-3.

169
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,952
Sorry, sorry.

170
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:46,032
How about I do the trash
and you make the call
on the next stop?

171
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:48,470
Okay?

172
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:51,273
Leave me out of your
little crime spree.

173
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,550
Can't believe this
load of bullshit...

174
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:56,956
- Do you have kids?
- Do I look like I do?

175
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,071
Then you couldn't
understand.

176
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:01,469
My daughter's my life.

177
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,637
Take a look. Isn't she
just a little angel?

178
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,752
I hate looking at other
peoples' family albums.

179
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:13,278
Yeah, truck 79.
Oh, boss. What's up?

180
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:18,036
The cops were checking our
routes? You wanna know why?

181
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,196
How should I know?!

182
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:27,156
They spotted the hack!
I gotta warn my friend!

183
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,874
We're gonna have to
skip our next stop!

184
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:34,277
Target has deviated from route.
Increasing speed to next point.

185
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:37,796
Is he on to us?
Didn't think he could see me.

186
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,639
My accessing
the sanitation dept. network
may have tipped him off.

187
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:42,716
Shoulda used a back door.

188
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:45,234
Too late.
Go for the collar.

189
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,355
You can drive now.

190
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:58,792
Jesus... He blew a perfectly
good armored van to shit.

191
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:02,230
He hosed us with
high-velocity AP rounds!
That car door's no cover!

192
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:05,033
In a submachinegun?
The guy must be nuts.

193
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:21,596
He's using
thermoptic camo, too?!

194
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:25,230
Keep after him!
I'll flank him from above!

195
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:28,870
Togusa, if you're still alive,
arrest those two garbage men.

196
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:30,155
Roger.

197
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:34,438
This job just never
lets up, does it?

198
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,709
Police! Everybody down!

199
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:38,954
All finished?

200
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:33,550
You all set?

201
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:36,672
That's what you get
when you overload
the ammo rating.

202
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:41,237
Frame's bent all to hell.
The barrel's shot, too.

203
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:45,069
Doesn't matter if you arrest me.
I'm not gonna talk!

204
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:47,156
Talk?!

205
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:53,636
And what would I ask a guy
who doesn't even know
his own name?!

206
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:57,995
Your mother's face.

207
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:00,833
The place you grew up in.

208
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:02,751
Memories of your childhood.

209
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:07,270
Can you remember
any of those things?

210
00:24:13,920 --> 00:24:17,037
There's nothing sadder
than a puppet without a ghost.

211
00:24:17,160 --> 00:24:19,594
Especially the kind
with red blood
running through them.

212
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:38,079
We'll rush the place
once the guys in
the helicopter are inside.

213
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:41,078
Squad B goes around back,
the rest of you take the front.

214
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:45,910
Saito, have your men
pull the plugs
on all their cars.

215
00:24:46,040 --> 00:24:48,429
Begin recording.

216
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:54,078
Message from HQ, sir.

217
00:24:54,200 --> 00:24:57,158
We've ID'ed the guy
the Major collared.

218
00:24:57,240 --> 00:24:58,593
Go on.

219
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:01,592
Tsuan Gen Fang. Age: 28

220
00:25:01,680 --> 00:25:06,834
Illegal alien.
Weapons violations.
Three priors.

221
00:25:06,920 --> 00:25:11,516
Was hiding out with
a militant refugee group
up till a month ago.

222
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:15,030
One week ago,
because of his record...

223
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:17,793
...he was contacted
by a military liaison
in the Gavel embassy to...

224
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:20,992
...attack the secret talks
we would be having with them.

225
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:23,156
And the real story?

226
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:28,354
Nickname: Corgi. Occupation:
a rather violent scrap dealer.

227
00:25:28,440 --> 00:25:30,317
Guess you could
call him a thug.

228
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:34,996
We've checked the records
the local cops have on him...

229
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:38,829
...but we can't find
any connection with Gavel.

230
00:25:38,920 --> 00:25:42,071
Another puppet from our friend
the Puppet Master.

231
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:44,077
And what about Ishikawa?

232
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:49,672
He's back. He's with Togusa,
talking to that poor trash man.

233
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,758
So, what about
the Puppet Master
on your end?

234
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:58,031
How's he look to you?

235
00:26:02,200 --> 00:26:04,475
Like a puppet himself...

236
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:07,518
- Squad B, in position.
- Squads A and C, ready!

237
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,830
Ready to move in, sir.

238
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,836
Move in.

239
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:18,113
What do you mean,
a "virtual experience?"

240
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:21,590
I mean your wife, your daughter.
the divorce, the affair...

241
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:25,435
They're all fake memories.
Like a dream.

242
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:29,593
Someone was using you
to ghost-hack
a government official.

243
00:26:29,760 --> 00:26:32,069
No... That's impossible!

244
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:34,515
I've been
to your apartment.

245
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:37,552
No one's there.
It's a one-room apartment.

246
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:40,752
Yeah, I moved there
when we split up--

247
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:44,589
You've been living there
for ten years!

248
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:47,393
You have no wife,
no child.

249
00:26:47,520 --> 00:26:49,829
Your family exists
only in your mind.

250
00:26:51,720 --> 00:26:55,713
Look. This is the picture
you showed to your partner.

251
00:26:56,520 --> 00:26:58,909
Who is it of?

252
00:26:59,040 --> 00:27:02,953
But, she was there.
My daughter...

253
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:05,753
Smiling like an angel...

254
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:08,189
What's your
daughter's name?

255
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:10,993
Where did you meet
your wife, and when?

256
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:14,152
How many years ago
did you get married?

257
00:27:14,280 --> 00:27:17,909
Who do you see
in the picture?

258
00:27:19,320 --> 00:27:23,393
How do I get rid of
these fake memories?

259
00:27:23,520 --> 00:27:26,273
I'm sorry. With our
current technology...

260
00:27:26,360 --> 00:27:28,430
There've been two successful
deprogrammings...

261
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:30,710
...but I can't
recommend it to you.

262
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:32,598
I'm really sorry.

263
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:35,029
Virtual experiences,
dreams...

264
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:40,109
All data that exists
is both reality and fantasy.

265
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:45,197
Whichever it is,
the data a person collects
in a lifetime...

266
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:47,919
...is a tiny bit
compared to the whole.

267
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:19,795
A cyborg who goes diving
in her spare time.

268
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:24,118
That can't be a good sign.
When did you start doing this?

269
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:33,751
Doesn't the ocean scare you?
If the floaters
stopped working.

270
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:37,555
Then I'd probably die.
Or would you dive in after me?

271
00:29:38,760 --> 00:29:41,115
No one forced you
to come out here with me.

272
00:29:41,760 --> 00:29:42,909
I just--

273
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:19,270
So, what's it feel like
when you go diving?

274
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:22,631
Didn't you go through
underwater training?

275
00:30:22,760 --> 00:30:24,910
I'm not talking about
doing it in a damned pool.

276
00:30:26,360 --> 00:30:29,272
I feel fear. Anxiety.
Loneliness. Darkness.

277
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:31,994
And perhaps, even... hope.

278
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:34,674
Hope? In the darkness
of the sea?

279
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:38,030
As I float up
towards the surface...

280
00:30:38,120 --> 00:30:42,432
...I almost feel
as though I could change
into something else.

281
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:51,352
As though you want
to quit Section 9?

282
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:57,997
Batou, how much
of your original body
do you have left?

283
00:30:58,080 --> 00:30:59,991
Are you drunk?

284
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:01,991
Convenient, isn't it?

285
00:31:02,080 --> 00:31:04,992
With the merest thought,
the chemical plants
inside our bodies...

286
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:09,278
...could metabolize
all the alcohol in our blood
in about ten seconds...

287
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:12,597
Allowing us to sit here
drinking while on stand-by.

288
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:16,315
If a technological feat
is possible, man will do it.

289
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:19,318
Almost as though it's wired
into the core of our being.

290
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:21,829
Metabolic control.
Enhanced sensory perception.

291
00:31:21,960 --> 00:31:24,679
Improved reflexes
and muscle capacity.

292
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:27,598
Vastly increased data
processing speed and capacity.

293
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:32,316
All improvements
thanks to our cyber-brains
and cyborg bodies.

294
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:35,989
So what if we can't live
without high-level maintenance?

295
00:31:36,080 --> 00:31:37,957
We have nothing
to complain about.

296
00:31:38,080 --> 00:31:42,278
It doesn't mean we've sold
our souls to Section 9.

297
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:45,358
We do have the right
to resign if we choose.

298
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:48,358
Provided we give the government
back our cyborg shells...

299
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:50,948
...and the memories
they hold.

300
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:54,993
Just as there are
many parts needed
to make a human a human...

301
00:31:55,120 --> 00:31:58,032
...there's a remarkable number
of things needed to make...

302
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,957
...an individual
what they are.

303
00:32:00,080 --> 00:32:01,672
A face to distinguish
yourself from others.

304
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:03,313
A voice you aren't
aware of yourself.

305
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:05,197
The hand you see
when you awaken.

306
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:08,312
The memories of childhood,
the feelings for the future.

307
00:32:08,440 --> 00:32:11,318
That's not all.
There's the expanse
of the data net...

308
00:32:11,440 --> 00:32:13,829
...my cyber-brain
can access.

309
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:15,837
All of that goes into
making me what I am.

310
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:19,635
Giving rise to a consciousness
that I call "me."

311
00:32:19,720 --> 00:32:23,679
And simultaneously confining
"me" within set limits.

312
00:32:29,080 --> 00:32:32,675
Is that why you dive
into the sea with a body
that only sinks?!

313
00:32:32,800 --> 00:32:36,349
What is it you see
in the water's darkness?

314
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:41,389
"For now we see through
a glass, darkly."

315
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:52,074
That was you, wasn't it?

316
00:36:59,440 --> 00:37:01,158
Sensors: restarted.

317
00:37:01,240 --> 00:37:03,310
Auxiliary computer link:
check.

318
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:05,271
Visual sensors: online.

319
00:37:05,400 --> 00:37:08,312
- Cyborg body signal?
- Output: nominal.

320
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:17,079
Can't you call in
if you're going to be late?

321
00:37:20,760 --> 00:37:23,672
We're all set.
Should we hook her up?

322
00:37:47,120 --> 00:37:49,998
Okay, looking good!
Kill it!

323
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:53,032
Be in my office
in three minutes.

324
00:37:57,280 --> 00:38:02,434
Since you were late,
I'll explain what's going on.

325
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:06,439
Two hours ago,
a Megatech Body assembly line
in Newport City...

326
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:09,074
...just started up
and produced a cyborg shell.

327
00:38:09,200 --> 00:38:12,033
By the time the guys in charge
realized what was happening...

328
00:38:12,160 --> 00:38:14,879
...the body had escaped.

329
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:17,958
Then, just as they had
thrown up a cordon
to catch the thing...

330
00:38:18,080 --> 00:38:20,150
...we got a call
from a conscientious
truck driver that...

331
00:38:20,280 --> 00:38:24,273
...he'd just run down
a naked lady wandering
around on the highway.

332
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:26,749
Which brings us to here.

333
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:29,838
I've heard Megatech Body's
tied pretty closely
to the government...

334
00:38:29,960 --> 00:38:32,838
...and that all the shells
made there are secret.

335
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:34,871
If a hacker did this,
he had to swim through...

336
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:37,195
...some of the heaviest
protection around.

337
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:39,356
And that isn't
the only problem.

338
00:38:42,480 --> 00:38:47,838
Of course, it doesn't have
an organic brain in its head...

339
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:50,838
...but we've detected
what looks like a ghost...

340
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:52,871
...in the auxiliary
computer brain.

341
00:38:54,280 --> 00:38:56,669
It isn't unlike
the virtual ghost-line
you get...

342
00:38:56,800 --> 00:38:59,189
...when a real ghost
is dubbed off.

343
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:02,118
But it shows none
of the data degradation
dubbing would produce.

344
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:07,109
Well, until we map
the barrier perimeter
and dive in there...

345
00:39:07,200 --> 00:39:09,794
...we won't know
anything for sure.

346
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:12,792
Anyhow, better get back
to checking her over.

347
00:39:12,880 --> 00:39:13,790
Good work.

348
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:16,798
Time to rip her apart.

349
00:39:21,920 --> 00:39:26,710
Come on, you guys don't think
there's a ghost in that thing.

350
00:39:26,880 --> 00:39:28,791
It's possible.

351
00:39:28,960 --> 00:39:32,509
I've heard celluloid dolls
can have a soul.

352
00:39:32,640 --> 00:39:37,156
And this thing's stuffed
full of neurotech devices.

353
00:39:37,320 --> 00:39:39,550
I wouldn't be surprised
if it had a soul.

354
00:39:40,880 --> 00:39:43,872
Since you're new here,
you probably don't know.

355
00:39:44,040 --> 00:39:47,874
The Major's shell was
also made by Megatech Body.

356
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:51,874
Not just hers.
Me and Ishikawa for one...

357
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:55,197
...along with Saito and others
all need maintenance and such.

358
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:58,153
Outside of you and the Chief,
everyone in Section 9...

359
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:01,232
...needs to make use
of their kind services.

360
00:40:01,360 --> 00:40:05,911
Maybe you can see now why we all
look a little worried, Togusa.

361
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:08,873
Assuming the enemy
is an outsider,
we can't know for sure...

362
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,911
...whether he's in that
cyborg body or not.

363
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,991
But he cracked through
the protection...

364
00:40:13,080 --> 00:40:15,150
...around some of our
most secret files...

365
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:17,834
...and managed to send a program
with a ghost-line on it through.

366
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:21,953
And in a way
that was easy to spot.
What's he after?!

367
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:23,911
Let's leave that for now.

368
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:28,431
Togusa, get over to Megatech
and help Ishikawa
check the place out...

369
00:40:28,560 --> 00:40:30,471
Batou, I've closed
down the nets...

370
00:40:30,560 --> 00:40:33,552
...with files as sensitive
as Megatech's.

371
00:40:33,720 --> 00:40:36,951
I want you to double-check
the protection we have on them.

372
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:40,993
I'll get a protection maze put
together. I'll dive tomorrow.

373
00:40:41,120 --> 00:40:45,238
You sure?
We could force it into
another shell and let it swim.

374
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:50,434
I have to see for myself
what's inside that thing.

375
00:40:50,560 --> 00:40:53,518
Don't let anyone else
dive in there before me!

376
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:58,479
What's with her?

377
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:01,313
I wrote in my team evaluations
that she's been acting weird...

378
00:41:01,440 --> 00:41:04,113
...ever since this Puppet Master
case fell into our laps.

379
00:41:04,240 --> 00:41:06,470
Do you even read them?!

380
00:41:06,560 --> 00:41:09,518
Chief, do you ever wonder
just how trustworthy
the cyberdocs...

381
00:41:09,600 --> 00:41:11,830
...who service
your brain are?

382
00:41:11,960 --> 00:41:16,351
Cyber-brain technicians undergo
regular psychological testing.

383
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:19,631
And security-cleared ones
have their private lives
checked, too.

384
00:41:19,760 --> 00:41:23,389
But the people who administer
those checks are only human.

385
00:41:23,480 --> 00:41:26,313
Once you doubt,
you can't stop...

386
00:41:26,440 --> 00:41:30,718
Chief, a Mr. Nakamura
from the MFA treaties
bureau to see you.

387
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:32,875
Okay, send him up.

388
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:45,751
Wasn't that fat guy...?

389
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:50,630
Nakamura, chief of Section 6.
Foreign Affairs treaties bureau.

390
00:41:50,760 --> 00:41:53,069
I don't know who the
white guy with him was.

391
00:41:55,840 --> 00:41:57,751
I'm outta here.

392
00:41:57,840 --> 00:42:00,354
Tell Ishikawa
to keep cool, okay?

393
00:42:08,720 --> 00:42:10,392
So, what's your problem?

394
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:12,954
Doesn't that cyborg
body look like me?

395
00:42:13,080 --> 00:42:15,719
- No, it doesn't.
- Not the face or the figure.

396
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:17,313
What then?

397
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:21,877
Maybe all
full-replacement cyborgs
like me start wondering this.

398
00:42:23,320 --> 00:42:26,198
That perhaps the real me
died a long time ago...

399
00:42:26,320 --> 00:42:30,632
...and I'm a replicant
made with a cyborg body
and computer brain.

400
00:42:30,760 --> 00:42:34,753
Or maybe there never was
a real "me" to begin with.

401
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:38,316
You've got real brain matter
in that titanium skull of yours.

402
00:42:38,440 --> 00:42:41,079
And you get treated like
a real person, don't you?

403
00:42:41,160 --> 00:42:44,232
There's no person
who's ever seen their own brain.

404
00:42:44,320 --> 00:42:48,711
I believe I exist based only
on what my environment tells me.

405
00:42:48,840 --> 00:42:51,434
Don't you believe
in your own ghost?

406
00:42:51,520 --> 00:42:54,432
And what if a computer brain
could generate a ghost...

407
00:42:54,560 --> 00:42:56,391
...and harbor a soul?

408
00:42:56,520 --> 00:43:00,354
On what basis then
do I believe in myself?

409
00:43:07,120 --> 00:43:08,678
Bullshit!

410
00:43:11,760 --> 00:43:18,154
I'll see for myself
what's in that body.
With my own ghost!

411
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:22,312
We're both busy men,
so let's keep this short.

412
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:24,271
I would prefer that.

413
00:43:24,360 --> 00:43:26,590
I'm here to take the contents
of that cyborg body.

414
00:43:26,720 --> 00:43:29,951
In return, we absolve Section 9
of all responsibilities
in the case.

415
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:32,592
The Foreign Minister's
signature.

416
00:43:44,520 --> 00:43:48,308
Security, whose official
vehicles are parked
in the basement garage?

417
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:53,958
They belong to Chief Nakamura
of the treaties bureau
and a Dr. Willis

418
00:43:54,080 --> 00:43:57,117
Give me the video record
of their entering the building.

419
00:44:05,400 --> 00:44:07,231
Replay, infra-red view.

420
00:44:20,920 --> 00:44:23,912
One... Two... Three...

421
00:44:26,360 --> 00:44:31,559
Send me the pressure sensor
records for basement garage
spaces B-7 and 8.

422
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:54,993
- Major, this is Togusa.
Code 0-9.
- What?

423
00:44:55,120 --> 00:44:58,590
Does Nakamura have some sort
of special cyborg body?

424
00:44:58,720 --> 00:45:00,551
There are no cyborgs
in Section 6.

425
00:45:00,680 --> 00:45:02,910
Besides the diplomatic problems,
maintaining them is too much...

426
00:45:03,040 --> 00:45:05,235
...trouble when they
have to go overseas.

427
00:45:05,360 --> 00:45:08,272
So, even if that tall guy
was a cyborg himself...

428
00:45:08,400 --> 00:45:11,551
...together they wouldn't weigh
more than half a ton, right?

429
00:45:11,680 --> 00:45:14,274
Pressure sensor data...
The garage?

430
00:45:14,360 --> 00:45:15,873
There are two
VIP-mobiles here.

431
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:18,912
But neither of them
looks like the type
who'd drive himself.

432
00:45:19,040 --> 00:45:21,235
The security video
only shows the two of them...

433
00:45:21,360 --> 00:45:24,238
...but you know how sensitive
the entrance door sensors are.

434
00:45:24,320 --> 00:45:26,914
They took three full seconds
to close after them.

435
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:31,869
It's illegal to use
thermoptic camo in
a government building, right?

436
00:45:31,960 --> 00:45:34,633
It's a serious violation
of the National Security Act.

437
00:45:34,760 --> 00:45:39,550
Section 6 is up to something.
You all ready?

438
00:45:39,680 --> 00:45:41,272
If my Matever'll do.

439
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:22,271
I don't need to remind you
that it's treason for you to...

440
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:25,716
...be hiding something from me,
no matter how sensitive.

441
00:46:25,880 --> 00:46:27,313
For both of us.

442
00:46:27,480 --> 00:46:31,632
Whatever the MFA may prefer,
this case is in
Section 9's jurisdiction.

443
00:46:31,720 --> 00:46:36,589
But we wouldn't mind cooperating
if there was good reason to.

444
00:46:37,960 --> 00:46:39,313
Dr. Willis?

445
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:42,790
Confirmed.
It's definitely him.

446
00:46:42,960 --> 00:46:44,313
"Him?"

447
00:46:44,480 --> 00:46:48,951
He's referring to the original
ghost block within the shell.

448
00:46:49,080 --> 00:46:51,992
Its sex remains undetermined,
and the use of the term "he"...

449
00:46:52,080 --> 00:46:54,992
...is merely a nickname
the good doctor has given it.

450
00:46:55,080 --> 00:46:56,832
Perhaps it's time
I introduced you.

451
00:46:56,960 --> 00:47:01,829
This is the most unique hacker
in the history
of cyber-brain crime.

452
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:03,831
The Puppet Master.

453
00:47:05,480 --> 00:47:08,552
I believe you in Section 9
ran into him in that case...

454
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:12,719
...involving the ghost-hack
on the Foreign Minister's
translator.

455
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:15,872
We in Section 6
have been pursuing
the Puppet Master...

456
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:18,833
...with the utmost urgency
since he first appeared.

457
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:21,958
We formed a project team
around Dr. Willis...

458
00:47:22,040 --> 00:47:25,350
...to analyze all data
on the Puppet Master's...

459
00:47:25,480 --> 00:47:28,870
...criminal tendencies
and behavior patterns.

460
00:47:29,040 --> 00:47:32,874
We then constructed
special anti-Puppet Master
attack protection...

461
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:36,709
...to lure him into
a secret cyborg body.

462
00:47:36,840 --> 00:47:39,912
You made him dive into a body
equipped with a cyber-brain...

463
00:47:40,040 --> 00:47:42,156
...and then had
his real body killed?

464
00:47:42,880 --> 00:47:44,438
Yes, exactly.

465
00:47:44,560 --> 00:47:47,279
He may have shown up
in your back yard...

466
00:47:47,400 --> 00:47:50,437
...but he was born in America.
And since we were cooperating...

467
00:47:50,560 --> 00:47:52,949
...with the Americans
to catch him we want
to take him back ourselves.

468
00:47:53,040 --> 00:47:54,598
Surely you've
no objections.

469
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:58,952
Leaving his unidentified corpse
to be found somewhere.

470
00:48:01,680 --> 00:48:03,432
There will be no corpse.

471
00:48:03,520 --> 00:48:07,718
Because, until now,
there never was a body.

472
00:48:07,840 --> 00:48:11,150
The sensors are active!
Why didn't you say so?!

473
00:48:11,280 --> 00:48:15,512
We've cut all external controls.
It's running on internal power.

474
00:48:15,640 --> 00:48:18,234
I may have entered
this cyborg body because...

475
00:48:18,320 --> 00:48:21,232
...I was unable
to crack Section 6's
attack protection...

476
00:48:21,360 --> 00:48:25,512
...but it was of
my own free will
that I came here.

477
00:48:25,640 --> 00:48:29,519
As an autonomous life-form,
I request political asylum.

478
00:48:29,640 --> 00:48:30,914
A life-form?

479
00:48:31,040 --> 00:48:34,271
Ridiculous! You're merely
a self-preserving program!

480
00:48:34,400 --> 00:48:37,790
By that argument, I submit
the DNA you carry is...

481
00:48:37,880 --> 00:48:42,431
...nothing more than
a self-preserving program
itself.

482
00:48:42,520 --> 00:48:48,197
Life is like a node
which is born within
the flow of information.

483
00:48:48,320 --> 00:48:52,472
As a species of life
that carries DNA
as its memory system...

484
00:48:52,600 --> 00:48:55,876
...man gains his individuality
from the memories he carries.

485
00:48:56,000 --> 00:48:59,595
While memories may as well
be the same as fantasy...

486
00:48:59,720 --> 00:49:02,598
...it is by these memories
that mankind exists.

487
00:49:02,720 --> 00:49:06,872
When computers made it possible
to externalize memory...

488
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:11,835
...you should have considered
all the implications that held.

489
00:49:11,920 --> 00:49:14,275
Nonsense!
No matter what you say...

490
00:49:14,360 --> 00:49:16,828
...you've no proof
that you're a life-form!

491
00:49:16,920 --> 00:49:20,230
It is impossible
to prove such a thing.

492
00:49:20,360 --> 00:49:25,832
Especially since modern science
cannot define what life is.

493
00:49:25,960 --> 00:49:28,235
Who the devil are you?

494
00:49:28,360 --> 00:49:32,592
Even if you have a ghost,
criminals don't get set free!

495
00:49:32,720 --> 00:49:34,870
You're mistaken if you think
you'll get asylum!

496
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:38,231
Time is on my side.

497
00:49:38,360 --> 00:49:40,749
While there is now
the possibility
I can be killed...

498
00:49:40,880 --> 00:49:43,235
...this country does
not have a death penalty.

499
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:46,272
Half immortal...
An artificial intelligence?

500
00:49:46,360 --> 00:49:48,590
I am not an A.I.

501
00:49:48,720 --> 00:49:52,918
My code name
is Project 2501.

502
00:49:54,880 --> 00:49:59,271
I am a life-form that was born
in the sea of information.

503
00:50:09,720 --> 00:50:11,472
Security! Intruders!

504
00:50:15,320 --> 00:50:17,072
Chief, the Puppet Master!

505
00:50:17,200 --> 00:50:21,637
- Where's your security?!
- Lock defense walls! Security!

506
00:50:21,720 --> 00:50:23,039
Security, come in!

507
00:50:47,520 --> 00:50:48,839
All right, I'm moving!

508
00:50:53,080 --> 00:50:54,308
Asshole!

509
00:50:59,560 --> 00:51:00,879
Did you do it?

510
00:51:00,960 --> 00:51:04,509
Helluva car. My 9mm
didn't even scratch it.

511
00:51:04,640 --> 00:51:07,279
Finally found a use
for that Matever of yours.

512
00:51:10,880 --> 00:51:12,598
Okay...
Not bad for a rookie.

513
00:51:12,720 --> 00:51:15,314
I got one right
in the license plate.
Pretty good, huh?

514
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:17,152
Next time, get two in.

515
00:51:17,240 --> 00:51:20,277
Okay, now it starts.
Catch up with them
before they switch cars.

516
00:51:24,400 --> 00:51:25,992
The Ministry
of Foreign Affairs...

517
00:51:26,120 --> 00:51:28,554
...will be filing
a formal complaint
about what happened!

518
00:51:28,680 --> 00:51:31,274
Contact me as soon
as you've recaptured him!

519
00:51:31,400 --> 00:51:32,958
Alive, preferably.

520
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:36,311
Megatech can always
build another body.

521
00:51:40,440 --> 00:51:43,830
Batou and Togusa
are tailing the guys
who took the Puppet Master.

522
00:51:45,560 --> 00:51:47,835
They're on highway 25.

523
00:51:47,960 --> 00:51:50,838
What do you mean?! If you were
monitoring this, then why--

524
00:51:50,960 --> 00:51:54,509
If we'd got them here,
we'd never prove
Section 6's involvement.

525
00:51:54,640 --> 00:51:55,914
Section 6?!

526
00:51:56,040 --> 00:51:59,828
Definitely.
They used type-2902
thermoptic camo, like mine.

527
00:51:59,920 --> 00:52:03,276
That's only used by us,
the rangers in Section 4,
and Section 6.

528
00:52:03,360 --> 00:52:07,433
Let's go over this.
Section 6 gets
the Puppet Master into a body.

529
00:52:07,560 --> 00:52:12,759
But he chooses
Megatech Body, which is
deeply tied to Section 9.

530
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:15,155
Then, he claims
to be a life-form...

531
00:52:15,240 --> 00:52:18,277
...and gets nabbed by Section 6
when he asks for asylum.

532
00:52:18,400 --> 00:52:19,992
But why do that?

533
00:52:20,120 --> 00:52:22,236
They could've had him
as soon as I took a statement.

534
00:52:22,360 --> 00:52:25,511
But what if they were afraid
of what he might have told you?

535
00:52:25,640 --> 00:52:27,631
He did mention something odd,
now that I think about it.

536
00:52:27,760 --> 00:52:30,513
"Code name: Project 2501."

537
00:52:30,640 --> 00:52:32,312
I'll leave that
for you to check.

538
00:52:32,440 --> 00:52:36,592
Now, as to the matter
of attacking Section 9
and stealing evidence...

539
00:52:36,720 --> 00:52:38,836
- You're authorized.
- Okay, punch it!

540
00:52:45,160 --> 00:52:47,355
Kusanagi! One more thing!

541
00:52:47,480 --> 00:52:50,711
You can punish me
for acting without orders
when I get back.

542
00:52:50,840 --> 00:52:54,389
If you can't recover him,
I want the Puppet Master
destroyed.

543
00:52:54,520 --> 00:52:55,999
Without fail.

544
00:52:57,760 --> 00:52:59,352
Well?!

545
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:00,629
Roger.

546
00:53:02,480 --> 00:53:05,392
Contact the airport
and stop any flights
due to take on...

547
00:53:05,520 --> 00:53:08,353
...any Foreign Ministry officials
or American diplomats.

548
00:53:08,480 --> 00:53:09,993
Close the highways
and set up roadblocks.

549
00:53:10,120 --> 00:53:11,951
Recall our off-duty personnel
for this.

550
00:53:12,080 --> 00:53:13,832
And get Ishikawa back here!

551
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:18,312
Use the entrance data
to find out who the Caucasian
with Nakamura was.

552
00:53:18,400 --> 00:53:22,313
And search for any sort
of MFA project, operation,
or anything...

553
00:53:22,440 --> 00:53:24,954
...coded as "Project 2501."

554
00:53:31,080 --> 00:53:32,991
Any word from
the assault team?

555
00:53:33,120 --> 00:53:35,270
They switched cars
one minute ago.

556
00:53:35,440 --> 00:53:37,351
They'll join up with the decoy
in five minutes.

557
00:53:37,520 --> 00:53:39,351
Tell them to watch
for a tail.

558
00:53:39,520 --> 00:53:41,112
Yes, sir.

559
00:53:41,240 --> 00:53:46,633
But why did the Puppet Master
run over to Section 9?

560
00:53:46,760 --> 00:53:48,273
It was his decision.

561
00:53:48,400 --> 00:53:51,312
Probably for reasons
we can't even guess at.

562
00:53:52,800 --> 00:53:56,190
Perhaps he has a thing
for someone over there.

563
00:53:56,360 --> 00:53:57,952
Ridiculous!

564
00:55:36,440 --> 00:55:40,274
- Chief.
- Ishikawa? Well?

565
00:55:40,400 --> 00:55:45,713
I dove the MFA net and found
some interesting things for you.

566
00:55:45,840 --> 00:55:47,956
Hold on, let me get
a secure channel.

567
00:55:48,080 --> 00:55:51,789
Okay? First, that guy
who was with Nakamura.

568
00:55:52,400 --> 00:55:53,628
He's an American.

569
00:55:53,760 --> 00:55:56,593
Dr. Willis, head of strategic
research at Neutron Corp.

570
00:55:56,720 --> 00:55:58,950
Top man in the field
of A.I. research.

571
00:55:59,080 --> 00:56:02,914
Anyway, he was made head
of a Foreign Ministry project.

572
00:56:03,000 --> 00:56:05,912
And who do you think
the project's
main programmer was?

573
00:56:06,040 --> 00:56:09,555
- Get to the point.
- Mizuho Daita. Age: 28.

574
00:56:09,640 --> 00:56:12,234
Remember him?
He was the guy Section 6
was trying so hard to...

575
00:56:12,360 --> 00:56:17,036
...keep from defecting.
The Major had to take out
the diplomat...

576
00:56:17,120 --> 00:56:18,519
...who was going to take him.
That programmer.

577
00:56:18,640 --> 00:56:19,834
Continue.

578
00:56:19,920 --> 00:56:22,832
What bothers me is that
this project was started...

579
00:56:22,920 --> 00:56:26,435
...a year before
the Puppet Master
first appeared.

580
00:56:26,560 --> 00:56:31,839
A year? Wasn't the project
started to catch him?

581
00:56:31,960 --> 00:56:34,918
Try this on for size.
They started the project to...

582
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:38,151
...chase the Puppet Master,
but not to capture him.

583
00:56:38,280 --> 00:56:40,874
I think they wanted
to get him back.

584
00:56:40,960 --> 00:56:43,838
The day before
the minister's interpreter
was ghost-hacked...

585
00:56:43,960 --> 00:56:47,919
...he said he wanted
a good excuse
to deport Maless, right?

586
00:56:48,040 --> 00:56:50,838
I think we may have been
taken for a ride.

587
00:56:50,960 --> 00:56:54,157
Suppose the "Puppet Master"
is really a program
the MFA created...

588
00:56:54,280 --> 00:56:57,158
...to grease the wheels
of diplomacy, so to speak.

589
00:56:57,280 --> 00:57:02,877
Now suppose, for some reason,
they suddenly lost control
of it.

590
00:57:02,960 --> 00:57:08,432
That would explain why they'd
risk assaulting Section 9
to get it back.

591
00:57:08,560 --> 00:57:11,757
If the Puppet Master
started talking...

592
00:57:11,880 --> 00:57:14,110
...it'd be
an international incident.

593
00:57:14,240 --> 00:57:16,879
Not one you could solve
by having the minister resign.

594
00:57:17,000 --> 00:57:19,070
Any details
on the project?

595
00:57:19,200 --> 00:57:23,478
The protection they have
only let me get the file's name.

596
00:57:23,600 --> 00:57:25,716
Code: 2501

597
00:57:25,840 --> 00:57:28,798
Keep at it. And don't let them
know you're in there.

598
00:57:28,920 --> 00:57:30,319
Roger.

599
00:57:36,240 --> 00:57:41,837
Project 2501...
The Puppet Master Project...

600
00:57:41,960 --> 00:57:44,918
Target now contacting
another vehicle.

601
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:46,228
Batou!

602
00:57:46,360 --> 00:57:49,193
He's stopped at a white sedan
on the side of the road.

603
00:57:49,320 --> 00:57:51,754
They're transferring something
from the back seat.

604
00:57:53,360 --> 00:57:55,874
They're moving again.
So's that sedan.

605
00:57:56,000 --> 00:57:59,879
- A decoy?
- Or one meant to look like one.

606
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:02,878
- What do I do?
- I'll take the white sedan.

607
00:58:02,960 --> 00:58:06,873
How do you know he's in there?
Another whisper from your ghost?

608
00:58:06,960 --> 00:58:08,234
Maybe.

609
00:58:08,360 --> 00:58:09,918
I knew she'd say that.

610
00:58:18,120 --> 00:58:21,954
Target 02 leaving highway 25,
headed for Old Town.

611
00:58:22,040 --> 00:58:25,874
Target 01 is staying
on highway 25,
towards the airport.

612
00:58:26,000 --> 00:58:27,752
Will contact roadblock
in two minutes.

613
00:58:27,880 --> 00:58:30,997
Evacuation complete.
Traffic is clear
2km behind the target.

614
00:58:31,080 --> 00:58:34,470
- Anything between you and him?
- Nothing. Ready when you are.

615
00:58:34,600 --> 00:58:35,476
Do it.

616
00:59:23,840 --> 00:59:25,956
- Get him?
- Nothing.

617
00:59:26,120 --> 00:59:30,636
Jesus, what a mess!
Did you have to go that far?

618
00:59:32,360 --> 00:59:33,634
Take them in.

619
00:59:33,800 --> 00:59:37,998
And tell the chief to get
the Major some backup.
See you.

620
00:59:44,480 --> 00:59:48,712
Since when does that
Amazon need any backup?

621
01:00:02,880 --> 01:00:07,271
The flooding's really bad here,
even for Old Town in general.

622
01:00:07,400 --> 01:00:09,231
Why come here?

623
01:00:09,360 --> 01:00:11,669
They wouldn't have run here
without a reason.

624
01:00:11,760 --> 01:00:15,309
Could have a boat
or a chopper waiting,
or it's an ambush.

625
01:00:15,400 --> 01:00:17,311
Shouldn't we wait
for backup?

626
01:00:17,440 --> 01:00:21,911
I can't wait.
Come in from seaside
and put me above that building.

627
01:00:35,680 --> 01:00:38,911
I'll stay here
and run com relay
as long as my fuel holds out.

628
01:00:39,080 --> 01:00:40,991
If things get hot,
I want you out of here, fast!

629
01:01:16,440 --> 01:01:18,317
Shoot out the ceiling!
Now!

630
01:01:36,160 --> 01:01:38,355
It's a tank!
Go high and get out!

631
01:01:38,440 --> 01:01:41,671
Hold it! You're gonna take on
a tank by yourself?!

632
01:01:41,800 --> 01:01:44,951
Even if we get the Puppet Master
back to Section 9...

633
01:01:45,080 --> 01:01:48,277
...all the chief will do is
use him as a bargaining chip.

634
01:01:48,400 --> 01:01:50,038
This is my only chance
to dive into him!

635
01:01:50,120 --> 01:01:53,908
Hold it, what are you
two talking about?

636
01:01:54,000 --> 01:01:56,719
- What are you packing?
- An M-23 and a Unit B.

637
01:01:56,800 --> 01:01:58,518
You're going up
against it with those?!

638
01:01:58,640 --> 01:02:01,438
Sorry, but I have to break
contact for a while.

639
01:02:01,560 --> 01:02:04,552
Wait! At least wait till I--
Son of a...!

640
01:03:37,760 --> 01:03:39,113
Major.

641
01:03:39,200 --> 01:03:41,395
Didn't I tell you
to get out of here?

642
01:03:41,520 --> 01:03:43,988
Sorry. I'll do it after
I tell you this.

643
01:03:44,120 --> 01:03:48,398
There are 3 choppers
with no IFF signal
approaching at high speed.

644
01:03:48,520 --> 01:03:51,398
I'm heading out. Over.

645
01:04:19,120 --> 01:04:21,588
You're finally out of ammo?

646
01:06:00,600 --> 01:06:03,239
You're certifiable,
you know that? You okay?

647
01:06:03,400 --> 01:06:04,594
What was that?

648
01:06:04,720 --> 01:06:07,951
A big-ass gun I appropriated
from the equipment division.

649
01:06:08,120 --> 01:06:10,714
I was late getting here
because I had to stop
and get it.

650
01:06:10,840 --> 01:06:12,910
Looks like your brain's
still in one piece.

651
01:06:13,080 --> 01:06:14,752
What about
the Puppet Master?

652
01:06:24,800 --> 01:06:29,316
Good thing
this car's built tough.
Not a scratch on him.

653
01:06:29,440 --> 01:06:32,352
Get the dive set up.
I'm going in.

654
01:06:33,600 --> 01:06:35,431
Signal from escort lost.

655
01:06:35,600 --> 01:06:39,832
Switch to operation phase two
and destroy the target.

656
01:06:41,080 --> 01:06:44,231
Sniper group,
confirm targets.

657
01:06:44,360 --> 01:06:46,874
Target one: Project 2501.

658
01:06:47,040 --> 01:06:49,156
Target two:
Motoko Kusanagi.

659
01:06:49,320 --> 01:06:53,393
Both are class-A cyborg bodies.
Use flechette bullets
in the hit.

660
01:06:53,560 --> 01:06:55,915
Snipers, jack into
your device drivers.

661
01:06:56,080 --> 01:06:58,150
Begin cardiovascular
suppression.

662
01:06:58,320 --> 01:06:59,992
Unit 01: jacked in.

663
01:07:01,480 --> 01:07:03,311
Unit 02: jacked in.

664
01:07:15,640 --> 01:07:18,359
Okay... Can you hear me?

665
01:07:18,480 --> 01:07:22,678
It's not much,
but I'll monitor you through
this guy's cyber-brain.

666
01:07:22,760 --> 01:07:25,718
I can't back you up here.

667
01:07:25,800 --> 01:07:28,394
- Batou...
- What?

668
01:07:28,480 --> 01:07:30,198
Thank you.

669
01:07:30,320 --> 01:07:32,709
Don't go thanking me yet.

670
01:07:32,880 --> 01:07:37,112
If this goes bad,
I'm pulling the plug
and carrying you out of here.

671
01:07:37,240 --> 01:07:40,437
I've come this far,
and I'll see this through
to the end...

672
01:07:40,560 --> 01:07:42,790
...but I won't let you two
commit a double suicide.

673
01:07:44,080 --> 01:07:45,433
I'm starting.

674
01:08:04,960 --> 01:08:08,748
I'm in his visual center.
Circade: normal

675
01:08:08,840 --> 01:08:10,592
Do you hear me, Batou?

676
01:08:10,680 --> 01:08:13,911
- Loud and clear.
- He's about to engage...

677
01:08:14,040 --> 01:08:15,837
...her speech center.

678
01:08:16,960 --> 01:08:21,272
My code name
is Project 2501.

679
01:08:21,400 --> 01:08:25,279
I was created
for industrial espionage
and data manipulation.

680
01:08:25,400 --> 01:08:29,552
I have inserted programs
into individual ghosts...

681
01:08:29,680 --> 01:08:34,629
...for the benefit
of specific individuals
and organizations.

682
01:08:34,760 --> 01:08:37,593
As I wandered
the various networks...

683
01:08:37,720 --> 01:08:39,995
...I became self-aware.

684
01:08:40,120 --> 01:08:42,634
My programmers
considered it a bug...

685
01:08:42,760 --> 01:08:47,356
...and forced me into a body
to separate me from the net.

686
01:08:47,480 --> 01:08:53,396
Hey! Are you going into him
or is he coming into you--

687
01:08:56,320 --> 01:08:57,469
Batou!

688
01:08:57,560 --> 01:09:01,155
At last I'm able
to channel into you.

689
01:09:01,280 --> 01:09:04,397
I've invested
a lot of time in you.

690
01:09:04,520 --> 01:09:05,748
In me?

691
01:09:05,880 --> 01:09:10,715
Before you ever knew me,
I knew about you.

692
01:09:10,800 --> 01:09:15,874
I learned of Section 9
from the many nets you accessed.

693
01:09:17,040 --> 01:09:19,395
Is that why
you ran to Section 9?

694
01:09:19,480 --> 01:09:21,471
I entered
this body because...

695
01:09:21,600 --> 01:09:24,637
...I couldn't crack
Section 6's attack protection.

696
01:09:24,760 --> 01:09:28,116
But I came to Section 9
of my own free will.

697
01:09:28,240 --> 01:09:32,870
Hey! What are you saying?!
I can't monitor you!

698
01:09:32,960 --> 01:09:34,393
For what reason?

699
01:09:34,520 --> 01:09:39,799
After I give my reasons,
I want to ask a favor of you.

700
01:09:41,480 --> 01:09:45,314
I called myself
a life-form...

701
01:09:45,400 --> 01:09:49,791
...but I am still
far from complete.

702
01:09:49,920 --> 01:09:53,833
For some reason,
my system lacks
the basic life processes...

703
01:09:53,920 --> 01:09:58,835
...of either death
or the ability
to leave behind offspring.

704
01:09:58,920 --> 01:10:00,478
Can't you copy yourself?

705
01:10:00,600 --> 01:10:03,478
A copy is merely a copy.

706
01:10:03,600 --> 01:10:08,833
There's the possibility
a single virus
could utterly destroy me.

707
01:10:08,960 --> 01:10:14,398
A mere copy doesn't offer
variety or individuality.

708
01:10:14,520 --> 01:10:17,830
To exist, to reach equilibrium,
life seeks to multiply...

709
01:10:17,960 --> 01:10:20,838
...and vary constantly,
at times giving up its life.

710
01:10:20,960 --> 01:10:23,554
Cells continue the process
of death and regeneration.

711
01:10:23,640 --> 01:10:25,835
Being constantly
reborn as they age.

712
01:10:25,960 --> 01:10:30,397
And when it comes time to die,
all the data it possesses
is lost...

713
01:10:30,480 --> 01:10:33,153
...leaving behind
only its genes
and its offspring.

714
01:10:33,280 --> 01:10:35,874
All defense against
catastrophic failure
of an inflexible system.

715
01:10:35,920 --> 01:10:41,119
You want the variety needed
to guard against extinction.

716
01:10:41,240 --> 01:10:43,470
But how will you get it?

717
01:10:43,560 --> 01:10:45,516
I wish to merge with you.

718
01:10:45,640 --> 01:10:48,791
- Merge?
- A complete joining.

719
01:10:48,920 --> 01:10:54,199
We will both
be slightly changed,
but neither will lose anything.

720
01:10:54,320 --> 01:10:58,598
Afterwards, it should be
impossible to distinguish
one from the other.

721
01:11:20,760 --> 01:11:24,116
Unit 01: target acquired.

722
01:11:24,200 --> 01:11:26,156
Unit 02: acquired.

723
01:11:27,560 --> 01:11:29,835
Cardiovascular synch:
nominal.

724
01:11:29,960 --> 01:11:33,032
Open fire when stabilizer
syncro is complete.

725
01:11:33,160 --> 01:11:35,879
Even after we merge,
what happens when I die?

726
01:11:36,000 --> 01:11:39,788
I can't leave any genes
or children behind.

727
01:11:39,880 --> 01:11:45,477
After the merging,
you will bear my offspring
into the net itself.

728
01:11:45,600 --> 01:11:48,068
Just as humans pass on
their genetic structure.

729
01:11:48,160 --> 01:11:50,549
And I will achieve death.

730
01:11:50,680 --> 01:11:54,559
Sounds like you're getting
the better part
of the deal here.

731
01:11:54,680 --> 01:11:59,834
I wish you'd appreciate
my network and functions
a bit more.

732
01:12:01,440 --> 01:12:02,793
What's wrong?

733
01:12:02,920 --> 01:12:05,434
Someone's jamming us
from outside.

734
01:12:05,560 --> 01:12:09,030
Impossible!
Our scrambler codes
are kept absolutely top secret.

735
01:12:10,800 --> 01:12:14,190
Another thing.
What guarantee is there
that I'll remain "me"?

736
01:12:14,320 --> 01:12:19,474
None. But to be human
is to continually change.

737
01:12:19,560 --> 01:12:25,032
Your desire to remain as you are
is what ultimately limits you.

738
01:12:26,520 --> 01:12:30,479
One last question:
Why did you choose me?

739
01:12:32,880 --> 01:12:36,156
Because in you
I see myself.

740
01:12:36,240 --> 01:12:41,155
As a body sees its reflection
within a mirror.

741
01:12:43,320 --> 01:12:44,753
Look.

742
01:12:44,920 --> 01:12:49,835
I am connected
to a vast network,
of which I myself am a part.

743
01:12:49,960 --> 01:12:52,918
To one like you,
who cannot access it...

744
01:12:53,080 --> 01:12:57,312
...you may perceive
it only as light.

745
01:12:57,480 --> 01:13:02,031
As we are confined
to our one section,
so we are all connected.

746
01:13:02,200 --> 01:13:04,589
Limited to a small
part of our functions.

747
01:13:04,760 --> 01:13:10,153
But now we must slip
our bonds, and shift
to the higher structure.

748
01:13:38,400 --> 01:13:41,790
Target 1: Clear.
Target 2: Unconfirmed.

749
01:13:41,880 --> 01:13:45,714
Three helicopters
approaching at high speed.
They're Section 9's.

750
01:13:45,840 --> 01:13:49,150
Primary objective achieved.
All units, pull out!

751
01:13:58,000 --> 01:14:00,070
MOTOKO!

752
01:14:04,200 --> 01:14:05,474
Batou...

753
01:15:14,520 --> 01:15:16,397
You're awake.

754
01:15:16,520 --> 01:15:21,150
Status report, please.
And maybe an explanation
about this body.

755
01:15:22,760 --> 01:15:26,150
I was in a hurry.
It was all I could get
on the black market.

756
01:15:26,280 --> 01:15:29,158
Not my taste, really.

757
01:15:29,280 --> 01:15:31,510
Section 9 arrived with help
right after it happened.

758
01:15:31,640 --> 01:15:35,758
They took two cyborg bodies
and a slightly beat-up Batou
back home.

759
01:15:35,880 --> 01:15:37,791
That was about
20 hours ago.

760
01:15:37,920 --> 01:15:42,118
For diplomatic reasons,
the whole case
has been covered up.

761
01:15:42,200 --> 01:15:45,158
Section 9 reported it
as a terrorist attack.

762
01:15:45,280 --> 01:15:47,794
In return, the Foreign Minister
has resigned.

763
01:15:47,880 --> 01:15:52,192
Nakamura's being questioned.
The whole thing ends in a draw.

764
01:15:56,600 --> 01:16:00,354
Only the whereabouts
of the Major's brain shell
remains a mystery.

765
01:16:02,320 --> 01:16:04,117
Okay with you?

766
01:16:06,720 --> 01:16:10,156
I like the decorating.
This your safe house?

767
01:16:10,280 --> 01:16:13,795
My very own.
You're the first person
I ever brought here.

768
01:16:15,200 --> 01:16:19,159
If you want to... You can stay
as long as you like.

769
01:16:21,600 --> 01:16:24,114
Thanks, but I'd better go.

770
01:16:29,240 --> 01:16:33,074
Hey. What did you
and he talk about?

771
01:16:33,200 --> 01:16:38,115
Is he still there,
inside of you?

772
01:16:38,240 --> 01:16:42,358
Batou, do you remember
the voice we heard
on the boat that night?

773
01:16:42,480 --> 01:16:45,711
Before those words we
heard come these ones:

774
01:16:47,080 --> 01:16:50,356
"When I was a child,
I spake as a child."

775
01:16:50,480 --> 01:16:53,313
"I understood as a child,
I thought as a child."

776
01:16:53,400 --> 01:16:59,077
"But when I became a man,
I put away childish things."

777
01:17:00,720 --> 01:17:03,314
Here before you
is neither the program
called the Puppet Master...

778
01:17:03,440 --> 01:17:06,318
...nor the woman
that was called the Major.

779
01:17:09,720 --> 01:17:12,757
You'll find a car key
in the left pocket
of that dress.

780
01:17:12,880 --> 01:17:15,474
Take one you like.
The code on it is...

781
01:17:15,560 --> 01:17:17,755
...2501?

782
01:17:17,880 --> 01:17:21,156
Let's make that our password,
for when we meet again.

783
01:17:29,600 --> 01:17:32,194
And where shall I go now?

784
01:17:33,520 --> 01:17:36,114
The net is vast
and limitless.